+	 * "write-combined".  Because this region is inside the kernel's memory
+	 * map, pfn_valid() is true for it and ramoops maps it with vmap() and
+	 * pgprot_writecombine() (fs/pstore/ram_core.c
+	 * persistent_ram_buffer_map).  That is the right attribute and the
+	 * other two are both wrong here: mem-type 2 ("cached") would leave the
+	 * newest records sitting in the A9 D-cache at the moment the CPU wedges
